	This disk or ARC file contains the latest version of my SNOBOL4hacks in C.  This library of functions (and complete programs) simulateSNOBOL4's pattern matcher in a C-coded function set and includes acollection of utility functions and programs translated from SNOBOL4code in "Algorithms in SNOBOL4" by James F.  Gimpel (Catspaw, 1986. ISBN 0-939793-01-6, 0-939793-01-8 (pbk.), Catspaw's address is P.O.  Box1123, Salida, CO 81201 USA (303) 539-3884 - call or write for prices,etc.).	This code compiles and runs under either CP/M-68K V1.2 orOS-9/68000 V2.2.  It is written in pretty generic (K&R) C and shouldcompile and run under almost any C compiler and operating system.  Fullsource code is included, along with a makefile for OS-9/68000.			Robert Heller			FidoNet 1:321/153.0 (Locks Hill BBS)			ARPANet Heller@cs.umass.edu			BITNET  Heller@UMass.BitNet			BIX     heller			GENIE   RHELLER			CompuServ 71450,3432			Locks Hill BBS is up 24 Hours a day				at 1-508-544-8337 - 300/1200/2400 BAUD